# 0308 = 0307 plus the PHY pull-up/down BIST fix.
#
# Root cause (docs/123): the PHY U2 ACR3 register was left with bit12
# (ACR3_PUPD_BIST_EN) set.  The vendor TWRP keeps ACR3=0xc0040000 (idle) /
# 0xc0040200 (attached) with BIST clear.  With BIST on, an idle TX endpoint
# answers an IN with no handshake at all (host USBD XactErr, libusb -9);
# every session's first immediate read failed and the second open degraded.
# Live A/B on the 0307 image (EP0 probe w32 0x11e4031c):
#   0xc0041200 (both bits)  -> empty IN XactErr 1.5 ms
#   0xc0040000 (both clear) -> empty IN timeout (NAK) 303 ms; S1/S2 8/8
#   0xc0040200 (BIST clear, PU_DP set) -> empty IN timeout 312 ms;
#                                         S1/S2 8/8, reads 0.2-0.5 ms
# Fix: init clears ACR3_PUPD_BIST_EN (and keeps the pre-attach PU_DP clear);
# the attach step still sets ACR3_EN_PU_DP.  Final ACR3=0xc0040200.
# Banner gate: "RUBY USB: 0308 acr3_bist=0".
#
# Default cmdline: config/0308-boot.cmdline (= 0306 base, txreset=0,
# lpmfcp on, cfgnoflush off; 0307 low-ring off).
# patchset: 7c27c8f78297bf292c6e1c4d146cc048f44bca439eab0dfa1fcf79009b372107
#           (291 files, computed locally from baseline-mirror)
